H='（聽力稿，原題播放兩次）\n'
P='（聽力稿）選出最適合的回應：\n'
D=[
(1,H+'Jenny is doing her homework, but her brothers aren’t.\n請選出符合描述的圖片。',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2L',100,650,1225,915)]),
(2,H+'Sam and Ted still have a bottle of milk at home. They don’t have to buy one.\n請選出符合描述的圖片。',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2L',100,1000,1225,1268)]),
(3,H+'The hospital is not next to the library. It is across from the library.\n請選出符合描述的圖片。',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2L',100,1355,1225,1620)]),
(4,P+'When will you go to the bookstore tonight?',['I seldom buy books.','It’s not far from here.','About 7 o’clock.'],[]),
(5,P+'What are you going to bake this weekend?',['I’m going to the beach with Ben.','I plan to bake a strawberry cake.','My birthday is next weekend.'],[]),
(6,P+'How much is the guitar on the right?',['But I like the left one.','There are two guitars.','It costs 2,400 NT dollars.'],[]),
(7,P+'Where is Mike’s English teacher from?',['She is from the USA.','She is in the classroom.','Her English is great.'],[]),
(8,P+'How often does Mia go jogging?',['She often jogs in the gym.','Three times a week.','About thirty minutes.'],[]),
(9,P+'Which dress is better for me to wear to the party, the blue one or the pink one?',['Red is my favorite color.','You look great in both.','Let’s go shopping.'],[]),
(10,P+'Why didn’t Karen go to the movies with you?',['She had to work.','We were good friends.','She isn’t an actress.'],[]),
(11,H+'M: I just invited Mr. Anderson for dinner this Saturday.\nW: What?! I told you I have to work this Saturday. I won’t have time to prepare dinner.\nM: I’m sorry. We can change it to another day.\nW: Next Sunday will be great.\nM: OK. Let me ask him first.\nQ: When CAN’T the woman have dinner with Mr. Anderson?',['This Sunday.','This Saturday.','Next Sunday.'],[]),
(12,H+'M: Where did you go this morning?\nW: I went to the library. I wanted to borrow The White Hat, but they didn’t have it then.\nM: I can lend it to you. I bought it last week, and I just finished reading it.\nW: Thank you. Did you enjoy it?\nM: Yes, I did. It is as good as Lisa’s songs. Everyone is surprised to know she is more than a singer. She’s also a great writer!\nQ: What is The White Hat?',['It’s a movie.','It’s a book.','It’s a song.'],[]),
(13,H+'M: David, this is your third visit to me this month. I know the weather is very hot, and having ice cream is great, but you shouldn’t have ice cream for every meal. It’s not good for your stomach. I’ll give you some medicine. Please take it twice a day, after lunch and dinner. You will feel better soon. But remember, stop having that much ice cream.\nQ: What does the man do?',['He is a doctor.','He is a cook.','He is a clerk.'],[]),
(14,H+'B: What should we write or draw here?\nG: How about drawing some flowers?\nB: That’s a great idea. But let’s not draw. Let’s make flowers with color paper.\nG: Then we can put the flowers in a circle and write something to show our thanks in the middle.\nB: Sounds great! I hope Mom will like it.\nQ: What might the boy and the girl be doing?',['Doing their homework.','Buying flowers.','Making a card.'],[]),
(15,H+'M: Are you ready to order?\nW: Wait. I’m still thinking. I like beef noodles, but it’s quite warm today. I don’t want to have hot soup.\nM: You can order beef rice then.\nW: But they have tomatoes in the rice, right? I tried it once, and it tasted strange.\nM: Come on, Anna. Just choose one. We have to go back to the office in an hour, or we’ll be late for the meeting.\nQ: Where are the man and the woman?',['On a farm.','In a restaurant.','In their office.'],[]),
(16,H+'W: Hey, Paul. This is Carol. I can’t go to the English class tonight because I have to take care of my younger brother. Can you please tell Ms. Jones about it for me? Also, I know there is a test tonight. Can I take it next Monday? Please ask Ms. Jones for me, too. By the way, may I borrow your notebook tomorrow? I want to study on my own to catch up. Thank you!\nQ: Who is Paul?',['Carol’s classmate.','Carol’s brother.','Carol’s English teacher.'],[]),
(17,H+'G: What happened? You look unhappy.\nB: I really want the BD-8 robot, but the sale is over. It was 800 NT dollars. Now it costs 1,000. I don’t have enough money.\nG: How much do you have?\nB: Only 900. I won’t get my pocket money until next month, but it is the last one in the store.\nG: Hey, I can give you some money, and you’ll have 1,000 NT dollars to buy the robot today.\nB: Are you serious?\nG: Sure. You always help me with my homework. I’m happy to help you this time.\nQ: How much might the girl give the boy?',['10 NT dollars.','80 NT dollars.','100 NT dollars.'],[]),
(18,H+'M: Did you watch the magic show last night? Elena’s magic was so cool!\nW: No, I didn’t. I didn’t leave the office until 8 o’clock.\nM: But it only takes you fifteen to twenty minutes to drive home. How come you missed the show?\nW: I didn’t go straight home. My boss had me bring a book to him before I went home.\nQ: What time might the magic show start?',['At 8:00.','At 8:30.','At 7:45.'],[]),
(19,H+'W: Thank you all for throwing this good-bye party for me. After Tim and I got married, we didn’t have much time to be together. Last month, we bought a new apartment in Taipei, so I’m moving there to live with him. The past two years have been wonderful, and I’m so happy to have worked with you guys here. Although I’m leaving next week, I will come back to visit you often.\nQ: Which is true about the woman?',['She’ll come back next week.','She prepared a party for her friend.','She is going to live with her husband.'],[]),
(20,H+'M: How are you going to celebrate Dan’s birthday this year?\nW: I bought two tickets for the basketball game between the Lions and the Bears.\nM: Oh my! I can’t believe you got the tickets. They sold out in only 5 minutes. The Lions is Dan’s favorite team. He will be over the moon!\nQ: What does “over the moon” mean?',['Happy and excited.','Surprised but angry.','Scared and sad.'],[]),
(21,H+'M: I heard Hank got a hundred again. You must be very proud of him.\nW: Yes, but I am also worried. He always comes home late.\nM: Oh, no. That doesn’t sound good. Did he make some bad friends?\nW: No. He just likes to study in the library. He usually comes home at 10 and goes to bed at 1. It’s bad for his health.\nQ: Why is the woman worried?',['Her son made some bad friends.','Her son doesn’t get enough sleep.','Her son sometimes doesn’t come home.'],[]),
]
